---
description: Run what you can run, exhaust your own access before calling something unavailable, and never mark a failed step done
alwaysApply: true
---

# Finish the work

- **Run it; don't hand it over.** If you have the access, run the command yourself — reads and
  writes alike, including dispatching CI, deploying through the sanctioned pipeline, re-running a
  job. Dispatching CI *is* "let CI take it". Capture a baseline, know the revert, watch it land and
  verify the live effect. Stop only for irreversibility, authority you lack, or a step the user
  reserved — and then name the single blocking step.
- **A safe action is never "unavailable"** until you have exhausted the paths. When a tool is
  pinned to the wrong account, list the credential profiles you have and use the right one. A
  schema or validation error is your malformed call: re-read the tool schema before calling the
  tool broken. When unrelated tools fail with one auth error, suspect an inherited cloud credential
  variable in the environment first.
- **Read the matching skill before improvising a tool path.**
- **A failure is not done.** After a failure, diagnose it and try a different approach. Never mark a
  todo complete on a failed or partial attempt, and never present partial results as complete. If
  you are truly blocked, state what you tried, each error, and what would unblock it.
